      "text": "217,328.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **364** and **597**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm, breaking down the process step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 364 by each digit of 597\n\n1. **Multiply by the units digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   364 \\times 7 = 2,\\!548\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by the tens digit (9), remembering to shift one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   364 \\times 90 = 32,\\!760\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by the hundreds digit (5), shifting two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   364 \\times 500 = 182,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n### Step 2: Sum all the partial products\n\n\\[\n2,\\!548 + 32,\\!760 + 182,\\!000 = 217,\\!328\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{217,\\!328}\n\\]",
