      "text": "374,296.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **767** and **488**, we'll use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n### Step 1: Multiply 767 by the units digit of 488\n\\[\n767 \\times 8 = 6,136\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 767 by the tens digit of 488 (remember to add a zero at the end)\n\\[\n767 \\times 80 = 61,360\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 767 by the hundreds digit of 488 (remember to add two zeros at the end)\n\\[\n767 \\times 400 = 306,800\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add all the partial products together\n\\[\n6,136 + 61,360 + 306,800 = 374,296\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{374,\\!296}\n\\]",
