      "text": "937,646.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **947** and **988**, we'll follow a step-by-step multiplication process.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe can break down the multiplication into more manageable parts:\n\n\\[\n947 \\times 988 = 947 \\times (900 + 80 + 8)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\n\n1. **Multiply by 900:**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 900 = 947 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 8,523 \\times 100 = 852,300\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by 80:**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 80 = 947 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 7,576 \\times 10 = 75,760\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by 8:**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 8 = 7,576\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Sum All the Results\nNow, add all the partial products together:\n\n\\[\n852,300 + 75,760 + 7,576 = 935,636\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{935,\\!636}\n\\]",
